        {
          "id": "4ad0e699-c5d7-3bc8-bf56-6e08d8afe1e2",
          "content": {
            "id": "4ad0e699-c5d7-3bc8-bf56-6e08d8afe1e2",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "The Week in Numbers: Nvidia marches on, Formula One zooms",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: From Nvidia's fortunes easing AI bubble fears to a new investor for the Mercedes Formula One team.</p><p>This is the Week in Numbers</p><p>:: Week in Numbers</p><p>:: $65 billion</p><p>$65 billion is how much Nvidia expects for its fiscal fourth-quarter sales.</p><p>The world's most valuable company also announced third-quarter sales rose 62%, their first acceleration in seven quarters.\u00a0</p><p>Global markets have looked to the chip designer to see whether investing billions of dollars in AI infrastructure expansion has resulted in an AI bubble.</p><p>:: $135 billion</p><p>A $135 billion economic stimulus package was approved by Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi's cabinet.</p><p>It marks the first major policy initiative under the new leader, who has pledged to pursue expansionary fiscal measures.</p><p>It's also Tokyo's largest stimulus since the pandemic.</p><p>:: 81%</p><p>Xiaomi reported a near 81% jump in third-quarter profit.</p><p>It comes with the Chinese tech giant moving further towards electric vehicles.</p><p>Xiaomi is also the world's third-largest smartphone maker.</p><p>It said the quarterly growth was driven by EVs, AI and other new projects.</p><p>:: $82,000</p><p>Bitcoin fell to around $82,000 on Friday, falling to its lowest level in more than six months.</p><p>The decline comes amid a broad sell-off in riskier assets.</p><p>One analyst recently told Reuters that because cryptocurrencies generally move with the stock market, they haven't become an asset of alternative value to hedge against fear in other sectors.</p><p>:: 15%</p><p>A 15% stake in the Mercedes Formula One team is how much CrowdStrike CEO George Kurtz now owns.</p><p>It comes out of the one-third stake held by principal Toto Wolff.</p><p>No financial details were given for the personal acquisition but media reports last week said the deal valued the former champions at a record $6 billion.\u00a0</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: From Nvidia's fortunes easing AI bubble fears to a new investor for the Mercedes Formula One team.</p><p>This is the Week in Numbers</p><p>:: Week in Numbers</p><p>:: $65 billion</p><p>$65 billion is how much Nvidia expects for its fiscal fourth-quarter sales.</p><p>The world's most valuable company also announced third-quarter sales rose 62%, their first acceleration in seven quarters.&nbsp;</p><p>Global markets have looked to the chip designer to see whether investing billions of dollars in AI infrastructure expansion has resulted in an AI bubble.</p><p>:: $135 billion</p><p>A $135 billion economic stimulus package was approved by Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi's cabinet.</p><p>It marks the first major policy initiative under the new leader, who has pledged to pursue expansionary fiscal measures.</p><p>It's also Tokyo's largest stimulus since the pandemic.</p><p>:: 81%</p><p>Xiaomi reported a near 81% jump in third-quarter profit.</p><p>It comes with the Chinese tech giant moving further towards electric vehicles.</p><p>Xiaomi is also the world's third-largest smartphone maker.</p><p>It said the quarterly growth was driven by EVs, AI and other new projects.</p><p>:: $82,000</p><p>Bitcoin fell to around $82,000 on Friday, falling to its lowest level in more than six months.</p><p>The decline comes amid a broad sell-off in riskier assets.</p><p>One analyst recently told Reuters that because cryptocurrencies generally move with the stock market, they haven't become an asset of alternative value to hedge against fear in other sectors.</p><p>:: 15%</p><p>A 15% stake in the Mercedes Formula One team is how much CrowdStrike CEO George Kurtz now owns.</p><p>It comes out of the one-third stake held by principal Toto Wolff.</p><p>No financial details were given for the personal acquisition but media reports last week said the deal valued the former champions at a record $6 billion.&nbsp;</p></body>",
            "pubDate": "2025-11-21T10:59:18Z",
            "displayTime": "",
            "isHosted": true,
